WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.800
Some of the biggest franchises in video gaming
are getting long awaited sequels in 2017,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.130
including Mass Effect and Resident Evil.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.900
But one title is still conspicuously absent
from the release schedule: Elder Scrolls.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.369
Here's a look at why we haven't seen Elder
Scrolls 6.

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:17.680
Skyrim remastered

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.760
Elder Scrolls 5: Skyrim was one of the most
popular games of its generation.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.100
So fans were pretty excited when the game's
developer and publisher, Bethesda, released

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:31.860
a new, remastered version in October, 2016
to celebrate Skyrim's fifth anniversary.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.590
But if you were frustrated that the studio
was using its resources to remaster Elder

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.300
Scrolls 5 instead of working on Elder Scrolls
6, there's some good news: studios frequently

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.850
use remastering old games as a way to fine
tune the game engine for a new installment.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.739
Capcom did it with Resident Evil, and Naughty
Dog did it with Uncharted.

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:52.560
So there's a good chance that the remastered
Skyrim is actually a stepping stone towards

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.280
Elder Scrolls 6.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.910
Skyrim is still popular

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.510
While many games like Evolve and Titanfall
can die out over time due to diminishing player

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.070
bases, Skyrim is still going strong.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.890
In fact, even five years after its release,
Skyrim is still one of the top 20 PC games

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:08.950
on Steam.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.369
One big reason for this is that Bethesda has
embraced modding by the player community,

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:16.779
encouraging fan participation to keep gameplay
fresh and vital.

00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:21.259
And as long as Skyrim is still popular, it
takes the pressure off Bethesda, allowing

00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:25.899
them to take their sweet time perfecting every
detail of Elder Scrolls 6 before they release

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:26.899
it.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:28.310
Bethesda takes it slow

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.689
Bethesda isn't a studio that likes to rush
their games.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:34.810
The studio has built up a sense of trust with
their fans, and Bethesda won't be pressured

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.740
to release Elder Scrolls 6 until they are
satisfied with the game.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.119
Bethesda honcho Todd Howard said as much at
E3 2016.

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:43.759
"We think very long term.

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:46.670
We're not a developer that's going to rush
something like this out.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.369
When you think about what is the future of
that kind of game, we have a pretty good idea

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:51.969
of what that's going to be."

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:56.229
That attention to detail is one reason Fallout
4 took seven years to make.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:00.149
And it's why the company's in no rush to finish
Elder Scrolls 6.

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:01.950
Elder Scrolls Online

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.300
It's important to also keep in mind that Bethesda
did release a new Elder Scrolls game in the

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.119
years since Skyrim's launch.

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:11.750
In 2014, fans got their hands on Elder Scrolls
Online.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.219
Developed by Bethesda's corporate cousin,
Zenimax Online Studios, the Elder Scrolls

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:20.680
MMO was itself in the works for seven long
years, as everyone insisted on the highest

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.299
level of quality control to ensure it lived
up to the Elder Scrolls franchise reputation.

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:29.280
And since then, the game has seen the regular
release of new content, with six DLC packs

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.650
so far and counting.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.349
So it's not like they're just sitting around
doing nothing!

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:35.290
Technical difficulties

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:39.439
One big reason for the delay is the simple
fact that Skyrim was created to be compatible

00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:44.849
with the previous generation of consoles — y'know,
your PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360 — while

00:02:44.849 --> 00:02:48.250
Elder Scrolls 6 is presumably being developed
for the current generation.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.530
That probably won't sit well with the game's
legion of PC players, but there is a benefit

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.549
to the advance in technology, as it will allow
the developers to build the game at a higher

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:57.620
level for everyone.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.030
That is, once they have the technology to
make the game in the first place.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.120
Which they currently don't, according to Todd
Howard.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.380
"I could sit here and explain the game to
you.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.300
And you would say 'that sounds like you don't
even have the tech, how long is that gonna

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.300
take?'

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.239
And so it is something that's gonna take a
lot of time, what we have in mind for that

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:14.239
game."

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:15.819
The studio has other projects

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:20.519
So if Bethesda doesn't even have the technology
to make Elder Scrolls 6 yet, just what are

00:03:20.519 --> 00:03:21.730
they doing with their time?

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.109
Well, according to Howard:

00:03:23.109 --> 00:03:29.239
"We actually have two other large projects
we're also doing that are bigger than anything

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:31.069
we've done.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:34.459
People will probably hear about those even
before Elder Scrolls 6."

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:37.800
That's great news for fans of Bethesda and
video games in general.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.050
But not so great for fans dying to see Elder
Scrolls 6 any time soon.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.219
When will Elder Scrolls 6 come out?

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:47.790
Even the people working at Bethesda can't
seem to agree on when Elder Scrolls 6 will

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.790
show up in front of gamers' faces.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.400
In fact, there seems to be some debate over
whether or not they're even working on the

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.400
game at all...

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.750
Executive producer Todd Howard certainly seemed
to think so when he was asked about it at

00:03:58.750 --> 00:03:59.900
E3 in 2016.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.280
"Are you guys gonna do an Elder Scrolls 6?"

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:08.060
"I think that's kind of like the elephant
in the room always when we talk about anything.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.459
I think it's good in these moments to tell
our fans, 'Yes, of course we are.'

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:14.599
It's something we love…

00:04:14.599 --> 00:04:17.440
I have to be careful what I say."

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.680
However, just two weeks later, Bethesda's
head of PR, Pete Hines, took to Twitter to

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.389
tell everyone that they actually aren't working
on Elder Scrolls 6 at all, claiming that Howard's

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:27.810
comments were misconstrued.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.630
So for now, the only thing we can be sure
of is that everybody wants Elder Scrolls 6

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.630
to come out.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.790
And nobody knows when it will.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.639
Hopefully the whole franchise hasn't taken
an arrow in the knee...

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:41.669
(unfunny meme origin)

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:42.990
God what an awful joke.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.009
Please end me.

00:04:44.009 --> 00:04:45.080
Thanks for watching!

